updates.body:
We are sharing the status of individual components and services as of 6:10:
• Yandex Cloud Console and API are available;
• Compute: partially available;
• MDB: most HA database clusters have switched over; some may operate in read‑only mode or be unavailable.
• S3: available for reading, potential issues with writing;
• Managed Service for Kubernetes: we are assessing the status of regional clusters;
• Yandex Identity and Access Management (IAM) is available;
• Other services may experience disruptions – we will provide updates on their status later.
Communication channels with technical support may be unstable. Information on the status board appears with a delay. We recommend using alternative resource recovery plans on external platforms.

Updates on the operation of services and components as of 07:13:
• Yandex Cloud Console and API are available;
• Compute: partially available;
• MDB: most HA database clusters have switched over; some may operate in read‑only mode or be unavailable.
• S3: available for reading, write issues may be observed.
• Managed Service for Kubernetes: partially available;
• Yandex Identity and Access Management (IAM) is available;
• Yandex Monium is unavailable.
The team is working on restoring technical support communication channels. We recommend using alternative sites to restore resources.

The team continues to work on restoring and stabilizing key services. We’re sharing an update on the service operations:
Yandex Cloud Console and API are available;
Compute: partially available;
MDB: most HA database clusters have switched over; some may operate in read‑only mode or be unavailable.
S3: available for reading, but there may be issues with writing;
Managed Service for Kubernetes: available, but issues with individual clusters may persist;
Yandex Monium: unavailable;
Yandex Container Registry: operational;
Yandex AI Studio: services are partially available, more details about the status.
Security services are partially available, more details about the status.
The Yandex Cloud team is working to resume the operation of technical support communication channels. The main recommendation remains the same: please use alternative platforms to restore resources.

The current status of individual platform services:
Yandex Cloud Console and API are available;
Compute: partially available;
Managed Databases: the service is available, but difficulties persist with Managed Service for Apache Kafka®.
S3: available for reading and writing, with possible slowdown in operation speed.
Managed Service for Kubernetes: available, but issues with individual clusters may persist;
Yandex Monium is unavailable;
Yandex Container Registry is operational;
Yandex AI Studio: services are partially available, more details about the status.
Security services are partially available, more details about the status.
The operation of the technical support channels has been partially restored; we are working to speed up the processing of inquiries, but there may still be significant delays in responses. We have also temporarily suspended the issuance of quotas for additional cloud resources.
The next update will be released on October 11 at 13:00 Moscow time.
